STORY = {
    'tm_the_tunnel_opens': (
        "Thornclaw said you'd be the first one up the hill, and he was right. Three years that mouth has been shut, and you're the first outsider through it.\n\nTake this token so the others know I let you in. Climb past the waystation and through the Honey Galleries, then keep on along the passage past them all the way to its end. That's the door to Timbermaw Hold, our home. Elder Haldor's at the Great Lodge at the top of the Hold, and he wants to see who Thornclaw's been talking about.",
        "Watch your footing in the Honey Galleries. The floor's sticky, and it's sweeter than it looks.",
    ),
    'tm_the_shamans_who_turned': (
        "The Elder sent you to me, so you've seen the Hold. The Deadwood were Timbermaw once, and some of them were born up there. The fel got into them through the water, but it's their shamans who keep it in them. Every night they feed the fel to the rest, and every night the rest forget a little more of who they were.\n\nGo down the tunnel to North Felwood and south-east to Felpaw Village, and put the shamans down. I'm not asking you to enjoy it, because I don't.",
        "If one of them calls out a Timbermaw name before the end, tell me which. I'd like to know who it was.",
    ),
    'tm_what_the_water_carries': (
        "My spring's water comes down through the mountain from the north, and for three years the Moonglade side was shut and the water tasted of Felwood. It still does. Something from the Bloodvenom is getting into it.\n\nThe oozes at Bloodvenom Falls are made of that water. Bring me what's inside them, sealed, and I'll find out what it is. The falls are down the tunnel to North Felwood and a long way south, past Talonbranch Glade.",
        "Seal the jars twice. That water gets through anything once, and I've stopped trusting corks.",
    ),
    'tm_bears_at_the_mouth': (
        "The honey comes down from the Hold's hives in these crates, and every bear in Felwood can smell it from the tunnel mouth. The healthy ones give up. The Fel-Rotted Bears don't, and two of them came up the hill last week and took a crate and half of Bramblecoat's coat. I've kept bees since I was a cub, and I've never lost a crate to a bear until this year. Go down the tunnel to North Felwood and thin out the rotted bears, which wander all over the valley, so you won't have to look hard.",
        "If you see a crate of mine out there, leave it. The honey's spoiled once a rotted bear has had it.",
    ),
    'tm_seeds_of_the_fel': (
        "The Deadwood have started planting. They never planted anything before the newcomers came through, and now I watch their gardeners from the ridge above Felpaw, going out with full pouches and coming back with empty ones. Whatever they're planting, it isn't food.\n\nBring me their seed pouches before any more go in the ground, and put down their pathfinders while you're at it, because they're the ones who show the gardeners where to dig. Felpaw Village is down the tunnel to North Felwood and south-east.",
        "Don't open the pouches out there. Whatever's in them has been waiting to be planted.",
    ),
    'tm_deadwood_feathers': (
        "Every Deadwood wears a headdress, and every headdress has Timbermaw feathers in it, from when they still knew who they were. I burn them in the waystation's fire, so whatever's left of who they were comes home. I've burned hundreds, and I say a name over every one, even when I can only guess it. Bring me Deadwood Headdress Feathers from the Deadwood of Felpaw Village, down the tunnel to North Felwood and south-east. Bring me a handful whenever you have them, as often as you like.",
        "Keep them dry. A wet feather smokes instead of burning, and that doesn't feel like home.",
    ),
}
